{
  "info": {
    "name": "ServXauto API (v1)",
    "description": "Phone + OTP authentication for the three actors: user (customer), worker (mechanic) and workshop (partner).\n\n**Base URL:** `{{base_url}}` (default `http://localhost:3000/api/v1`)\n\n**Flow — two calls per actor:**\n1. `Send OTP` — checks the account exists, then sends a 6-digit code. No SMS provider is wired up yet, so in development the code is printed to the server console by SmsService (`OTP for +919876543210: 123456`).\n2. `Login` — verifies the code and returns `{ user, token, is_new_user }`. A test script saves `token` into the environment automatically.\n\n**`check_existance`** (optional, default `true`): `true` rejects an unknown phone number with 404. Send `false` to issue a code for a phone that has no account yet — `Login` then creates the account and returns `is_new_user: true`.\n\n**Dev shortcut:** when `NODE_ENV=development`, the code `112233` is accepted for any phone number, so you can log in without reading the console. That is the default value of the `otp` variable.\n\n**`phone_no` must be E.164** — `+919876543210`, leading `+` required. Spaces and dashes are stripped before validation.\n\n**Codes expire** after `OTP_TTL_S` seconds (300 by default) — `expires_at` in the response is authoritative, so drive the countdown from it rather than a local timer. Re-sending replaces the pending code, so only the newest one works, and is refused for `OTP_RESEND_COOLDOWN_S` seconds (30) with 429 `OTP_RESEND_TOO_SOON`.\n\n**Errors** all look like `{ \"status_code\": 404, \"message\": \"User not found\", \"error_code\": \"USER_NOT_FOUND\" }`. `message` is for display, `error_code` for client logic.\n\n**Auth:** these six endpoints are public. The collection sends `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` by default so future protected requests inherit it; each auth request overrides that with no-auth.\n\n**Not implemented yet:** no guard consumes the token, there is no refresh token, logout or `/me` endpoint, and email OTP needs Redis for the mail queue.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api/v1",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth / User",
      "description": "Customer login. Accounts live in the `users` table.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/user/send-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "user",
                "send-otp"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone_no\": \"{{phone_no}}\",\n  \"check_existance\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Sends a login code to `phone_no`.\n\n- `phone_no` — E.164, e.g. `+919876543210`.\n- `check_existance` — optional, defaults to `true`. With `true` an unknown number returns 404 `User not found`. Set `false` to register a new customer; `Login` will then create the account.\n- Re-sending replaces the pending code. The previous code stops working.\n- The code is logged to the server console in development; there is no SMS provider yet.\n- Re-sending is refused for `OTP_RESEND_COOLDOWN_S` seconds (30 by default) with 429 `OTP_RESEND_TOO_SOON`. Use `resend_after_seconds` from the response to drive the client countdown."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 — code sent",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
